      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I found that VCC was producing network errors in the Windows Event Viewer. I was able to temporarily fix this each time it happens by running these commands in an elevated terminal:\n\nnet stop winnat\n\nnet start winnat\n\nI have weird port issues like this relatively often and it appears likely related to an issue with Hyper-V where it will aggressively reserves various port ranges. So there may be an issue to work around there.\n\nhttps://github.com/microsoft/WSL/issues/5514",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64c87859e89e2e09549e6355",
